      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define the move schedule and resource plan across shifts.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Alright team, the initial mapping is looking good. Now we need to lock in the schedule for the actual moves. I've put together a first draft in A5 Move Schedule and Resource Plan, aiming to get T5 done. Please review and let me know of any conflicts.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "calendar",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 136230,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks @49303. Looking at A5, the proposed dates for the main office archive clash with our month-end financial reporting. We can't have that area disrupted from the 28th to the 30th. Can we move it to the first week of next month?",
            "mentions": [
              49303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 153021,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "The warehouse slots look mostly okay, but I see you've scheduled the heavy machinery zone for a night shift. We usually only have one certified forklift operator on at night. Is that enough?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Good catch, @136230. Yes, we can swap the main archive with the marketing storage room move. That should work. I'll update A5.",
            "mentions": [
              136230
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Re: the forklift, you're right. We'll need at least two movers plus the operator for that zone to be safe and efficient. Let's decide on the team size per batch. I propose 3 movers for warehouse zones and 2 office clerks for record areas. That should be our standard.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 112406,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "While we're on scheduling, have we thought about how we'll track the boxes in real-time? For T7, we need to set up the tracking log. I can create a simple sheet for A6, but we need to make sure everyone uses it during the move.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 136230,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "3 movers and 2 clerks per batch sounds right. That gives us enough people without overcrowding the space. I agree with that.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 304178,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "3 movers is good.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Good point, @112406. Please set up A6. We'll make it a mandatory step in the process: no box moves until it has a unique ID and is logged. We can cover that in the pre-move briefing.",
            "mentions": [
              112406
