      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Lock in safety, stacking and confidentiality rules before the pilot move.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, with the schedule set, we need to finalize our procedures before the pilot move (T8) next week. I've drafted the A2 Safety Checklist for T6. It covers lifting limits, stacking, and handling dangerous goods. Please review and add any comments. I've also sent it to the Health and Safety Officer for their official review.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T6",
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "safety_vest",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 153021,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "Looks comprehensive. The stacking height limits seem right for standard pallets. Good call on including the check for damaged racking before placing loads.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 304178,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "In A2 it says 'secure loose items'. For the big machines we have to move, what's the best way to do that? Just straps?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "Good question. For disassembled machines, all parts should be boxed or crated separately. For whole units, yes, use tension straps and check they are rated for the weight. I'll add a note to A2 to be more specific on that point.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 136230,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "Thanks for leading on safety, @49303. On the office side, we need to lock down the A4 Confidential Records Handling Rules for T4. I've written a draft based on standard data protection principles. The key points are: all sensitive document boxes must be sealed with tamper-proof tape, and access to the new archive room will be restricted. Please review.",
            "mentions": [
              49303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 112406,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "The rules in A4 look clear and easy to follow. Defining the access levels per record category is a great idea.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 53954,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "For T4, what does digitising mean? Do I just take a picture of the document with my phone?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 136230,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "No, please don't use your phone for that, it's a security risk. We must use the dedicated office scanner which saves directly to the secure network drive. I've specified the process in A4. Let's go over it together before you start.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "lock",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 53954,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "oh ok thanks",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "The Health and Safety Officer has approved the checklist with the clarification on securing machines. With that, I think we can approve the A2 Safety Checklist.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 136230,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "And it seems we have consensus on the document handling rules. Let's confirm the A4 confidentiality rules are approved so we can proceed with preparations for the pilot.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 112406,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Confirmed.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 49303,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Great. Now we're ready for T8. Let's make sure everyone reads A2 and A4 before their shift on pilot day.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8",
              "A2",
